    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0571" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1688</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2345</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-08">January 8, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received January
                        15.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 249 of December 29, 7 p.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d640-f1"/> authorizing me
                    to participate informally and independently in debt discussions with the
                    Brazilian authorities for the purpose of ascertaining what terms the Brazilians
                    are prepared to offer, I have the honor to enclose copies of a letter<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d640-f2"/> and memorandum that I have sent to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs<anchor n="3a" xml:id="d640-f3"/> following my recent
                    conversation with him on the subject mentioned in my telegram No. 461 of
                    December 30, 10 p.m.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d640-f4"/></p>
                <p>No discussions are being carried on with the Europeans at present.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to suggest that the Treasury Department be informed
                    appropriately.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d640-a1.xml" xpointer="d640-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
